WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:03.234
-Oh, I heard you missed us.

00:00:03.234 --> 00:00:07.567
We're back.
It has been too long.

00:00:07.567 --> 00:00:10.767
Five months. I love you guys.
I missed everything here.

00:00:10.767 --> 00:00:14.200
[ Cheers and applause ]
Oh, I miss it all.

00:00:16.767 --> 00:00:19.200
It was a long time.

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:21.801
Higgins, what were you up
to these five months?

00:00:21.801 --> 00:00:22.934
-I went to prison.

00:00:22.934 --> 00:00:24.767
[ Laughter ]

00:00:24.767 --> 00:00:26.234
-Roots, what'd you do?

00:00:26.234 --> 00:00:29.033
-We were in prison, too.
-Yeah.

00:00:29.033 --> 00:00:31.767
It's good to see you.
I spent a lot of time at home

00:00:31.767 --> 00:00:32.934
really is what I did.

00:00:32.934 --> 00:00:35.701
I was with the kids
all the time, so much.

00:00:35.701 --> 00:00:38.767
And this is --
Maybe this is a true story.

00:00:38.767 --> 00:00:41.267
So, I was leaving today
at breakfast. I go, "I'm going."

00:00:41.267 --> 00:00:43.434
"Where are you going?" I go,
"Daddy's going back to work."

00:00:43.434 --> 00:00:44.701
And they just started
applauding.

00:00:44.701 --> 00:00:46.634
[ Laughter ]

00:00:46.634 --> 00:00:47.968
I got a two-minute
standing ovation

00:00:47.968 --> 00:00:49.634
like I was at
the Venice Film Festival.

00:00:49.634 --> 00:00:52.801
[ Laughter ]

00:00:52.801 --> 00:00:54.334
I swear. They really did.

00:00:54.334 --> 00:00:56.300
I go, "Wow, was I
that annoying?"

00:00:56.300 --> 00:00:59.901
But actually, I started a
podcast in the five months

00:00:59.901 --> 00:01:02.234
with the other hosts.

00:01:02.234 --> 00:01:06.400
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:06.400 --> 00:01:08.067
The other late-night hosts,

00:01:08.067 --> 00:01:09.400
we started a podcast,
and all the money

00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:11.634
went to our crew and staff
who were out of work.

00:01:11.634 --> 00:01:13.501
And it was called
Strike Force Five.

00:01:13.501 --> 00:01:16.234
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:16.234 --> 00:01:20.267
And I really -- I really want
to thank Jimmy Kimmel,

00:01:20.267 --> 00:01:21.667
Stephen Colbert,
John Oliver,

00:01:21.667 --> 00:01:23.400
and our upstairs neighbor,
Seth Meyers.

00:01:23.400 --> 00:01:26.334
They're just fantastic guys.

00:01:26.334 --> 00:01:29.167
And I know them
and I'm friendly with them.

00:01:29.167 --> 00:01:31.033
But, you know,
I would say after this,

00:01:31.033 --> 00:01:32.868
I'm friends with them.

00:01:32.868 --> 00:01:35.901
And really, and they were
just great friends

00:01:35.901 --> 00:01:37.434
and great people to talk to.

00:01:37.434 --> 00:01:41.200
And it's a fun podcast
if you want to listen to it.

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:44.601
But we all get assigned
different shows, right, to host.

00:01:44.601 --> 00:01:47.634
And so I hosted an episode
called -- It was episode five.

00:01:47.634 --> 00:01:49.701
It was like a "Newlywed Game"
type of thing where --

00:01:49.701 --> 00:01:52.234
because we're all married
to great, great women

00:01:52.234 --> 00:01:55.400
and they must be going
through the same craziness

00:01:55.400 --> 00:01:57.067
that we all, you know,
we have a lot in common.

00:01:57.067 --> 00:01:59.667
So I did it through text.

00:01:59.667 --> 00:02:01.767
You know, I texted them
the questions and stuff,

00:02:01.767 --> 00:02:03.300
and it just was a disaster.

00:02:03.300 --> 00:02:05.367
[ Laughter ]

00:02:05.367 --> 00:02:08.267
Like I said, like, "When did you
first fall in love?"

00:02:08.267 --> 00:02:11.367
And so they were like --
they answered -- some answered

00:02:11.367 --> 00:02:13.567
for what they thought
their husband would say,

00:02:13.567 --> 00:02:14.934
and then some
of the hosts were like,

00:02:14.934 --> 00:02:16.968
"So are we guessing
what they're guessing

00:02:16.968 --> 00:02:19.133
we would say?"
I go, "I don't know.

00:02:19.133 --> 00:02:21.601
I just texted them
these questions."

00:02:21.601 --> 00:02:23.534
So I don't really know
the rules of the game.

00:02:23.534 --> 00:02:26.033
It changed a lot,
but you get to know everybody

00:02:26.033 --> 00:02:28.067
and it's good to see
that side of them

00:02:28.067 --> 00:02:31.167
and the human side
of the talk show host

00:02:31.167 --> 00:02:33.234
that we know
and see all the jokes,

00:02:33.234 --> 00:02:35.434
but got to really get
in there and talk to them.

00:02:35.434 --> 00:02:37.501
They're all smart
and great entertainers

00:02:37.501 --> 00:02:38.667
and great comedians.

00:02:38.667 --> 00:02:40.834
But I had a lot of time,
five months,

00:02:40.834 --> 00:02:43.467
a lot of time to really just sit
and think, you know?

00:02:43.467 --> 00:02:48.334
And I just finally
just took a moment

00:02:48.334 --> 00:02:51.200
and I just realized
how grateful I am

00:02:51.200 --> 00:02:53.400
for all of this
and for this show.

00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:54.534
I really love it.

00:02:54.534 --> 00:02:58.667
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:58.667 --> 00:03:02.601
I really --
I really love this job.

00:03:02.601 --> 00:03:04.534
I love doing it.
I love telling jokes.

00:03:04.534 --> 00:03:05.801
I love interviewing people.

00:03:05.801 --> 00:03:07.934
I love making you laugh.

00:03:07.934 --> 00:03:09.334
I'm very lucky
to have this show.

00:03:09.334 --> 00:03:12.567
And I want to thank you all
for supporting and choosing

00:03:12.567 --> 00:03:14.434
to have me
in your bedrooms at nighttime.

00:03:14.434 --> 00:03:15.434
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:15.434 --> 00:03:17.801
This is what I love to do

00:03:17.801 --> 00:03:19.534
and I want to do it
for a long time.

00:03:19.534 --> 00:03:20.901
I'm so happy to be back.

00:03:20.901 --> 00:03:22.400
Thank you to our crew,
our staff.

00:03:22.400 --> 00:03:24.501
Our writers
are now back in the building

00:03:24.501 --> 00:03:26.367
and we're going to make
some fun shows.

00:03:26.367 --> 00:03:27.467
[ Cheers and applause ]

